        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Eisei Meijin is a digital conversion of the traditional Japanese board game Shogi for one or two players, and the first game in Konami's long-running Shogi series to come to console. In addition to standard play against the computer or a second player, it includes the ability to record and play back matches, and even includes playable records of several historical Shogi matches from the Edo era. Also included are a board edit mode and a tool that automatically solves Tsume Shogi problems.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
